        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Just closed on a new home in Smyrna, DE? Before you finish unpacking, run through this Smyrna move-in locksmith checklist first. Smyrna is in the middle of one of the biggest new-construction booms in Kent County, with dozens of active communities under construction right now along the Route 13 corridor, from starter homes to 55-plus neighborhoods. Does a brand-new house actually need new locks? The short answer is yes, and here's exactly what to check.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#A61E22] bg-[#F8F8F5] px-6 py-4 my-8 not-italic">
          <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1 mb-0">
            <li>Smyrna currently has dozens of active new-construction communities from more than a dozen builders, so a fresh subdivision address does not mean a fresh set of keys.</li>
