        <!-- FAQ -->
        <h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-12 mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 not-prose">
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">Should I rekey a brand-new construction home in Smyrna, DE?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. A new-construction home in Smyrna typically has more outstanding keys by closing than a resale, once you count the builder's crew, subcontractors, the real estate agent, and anyone who toured the model or the finished home.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">Do Smyrna home builders keep copies of my house keys?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">In most cases, yes, at least through the closing process. Builders, site supervisors, and trade crews generally hold working keys until final walkthrough, which is exactly why a move-in rekey matters even on a house nobody has ever lived in.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">Is rekeying different from replacing my locks entirely?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. Rekeying resets the internal pins so old keys stop working while the hardware stays the same. Replacing swaps the hardware itself. Most Smyrna new-construction homes only need a rekey, not a full replacement. See our <a href="/blog/moving-into-new-home-rekey-or-replace-locks/" class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold hover:underline">full rekey-vs-replace breakdown</a> for the complete decision guide.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">How do I avoid overpaying a locksmith in Smyrna?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Ask for a firm quote before the technician arrives and confirm it in writing or by text. The Better Business Bureau has tracked a nationwide pattern of locksmiths quoting a low price online, then charging significantly more once they are on-site.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-2">What areas near Smyrna does 1st Capital Locksmith serve?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">1st Capital Locksmith serves Smyrna and the surrounding northern Kent County communities, including Clayton, Cheswold, Camden, and Wyoming, as part of our regular mobile coverage area. See our <a href="/service-areas/smyrna-de/" class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold hover:underline">Smyrna, DE service area page</a> for full details.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

